  "assumptions": [
   "About 300 per cell (6 cells, N about 1,800) to detect 0.04 at 80% power; H5 observed 0.066-0.091 with SE about 0.03; 300 per cell detects 0.04-0.05 at 80% power.",
   "Only two of the 20 items are shown in the schema as examples; the full instrument repeats the item/response pair for 20 items, drawn from pools with 4 or 16 AI items.",
   "Item order is randomised and the same authentic items are used across base rates where possible.",
   "A payoff-for-accuracy variant (bonus per correct answer) can be added as a robustness check.",
   "Platform: US online panel, about 10 minutes; d' uses a log-linear correction for extreme rates.",
   "Participants are not told the base rate."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
